-- Lost City of the Tol'vir: the trash had no link to a heroic copy (apart from the Oathsworn Captain), and the heroic copies were level 1 friendly
-- placeholders that nothing used, so the heroic dungeon had the stats of the normal one. The trash is linked to its heroic copy, the heroic copies get
-- the 4.3.4 values (level 85) and the heroic copy of a trash type that drops items (and the Oathsworn Captain, whose heroic copy had no loot table)
-- uses the loot table of its normal entry. The levels, damage and gold of the trash follow the 4.3.4 data; flag bits the core does not accept from
-- the database are left out. The bosses keep the values they have.
